patch 383 -- drop the 3 base-lost FAR reloc-applier stray dispatches (lcall [ds:0x12] = f842) reached at
BOOT -> eliminate the intermittent SIGSEGV that flakes EVERY verify flow (the 10x-gate blocker).

THE FLAKE (pre-existing, ~1-2.6%/boot native rc=139; the "cancel-flow 26de" attribution was WRONG): the
SEGV is at BOOT in FUN_0000_f842+0x56 (the FAR reloc applier, DGROUP:0x12), reached via app_entry -> the
driver-load init sequence 06bc/f7ad/4f6e/4b16.  NOT the cancel teardown, NOT m_mga 26de.  Because these run
once at boot before any screen, the flake hits EVERY flow -> THE flaky-flow blocker for the 10x-consecutive
gate.  Caught + core-confirmed on the ASLR-on layout (fault-addr a small near-offset ~0xff84/0xfff2 = the
classic near-offset-used-as-host-pointer base-loss; backtraces: f842<-4b16<-app_entry and f842<-4f6e<-app_entry).

ROOT (asm-cited, re_out/fist_dat_image.bin): each site is the real-mode idiom `[xor bx,bx;] mov si,<off>;
lcall [ds:0x12]` -- install a far method-vector section from the game's own reloc table (seg 0x3352:si) via
the far applier f842.  Ghidra rendered f842 INERT/base-lost (dropped its `mov es,ax; mov ds,bx` string-op
segment bases -> the C f842 executes `*(uint16_t*)dgroup_off = ..` with the near offset as a raw HOST
pointer) AND the indirect __allregs service call `(*DAT_1000_c012)()` drops SI/param_1/param_3.  So f842
runs on uninitialised cdecl-stack garbage: when garbage param_1!=0 and the (garbage) section pointer yields a
nonzero dgroup_off, it wild-writes to a small near-offset address -> SIGSEGV.  Doubly garbage-dependent ->
intermittent.  The three boot sites (0x14b16 si=0x274, 0x14f6e si=0x2b0, 0x106e8 si=0xec):
  * 4b16 (0x14b16): DGROUP:0x12 live by here -> f842 fired -> ~2.6% crash.  The faithful install of section
    0x274 is ALREADY done by the shim fist_apply_reloc_section(0x274,1) on the very next line (patch 022).
  * 4f6e (0x14f6e): DGROUP:0x12 live by here (after 06bc/f7ad) -> f842 fired -> THE residual crash after the
    4b16 fix (core: f842<-4f6e<-app_entry).  Section 0x2b0 is installed nowhere else; this dispatch never
    performed the install faithfully (garbage param_1: crash, or param_1==0 -> the far-CLEAR f7c3).
  * 06bc (0x106e8, C line 40991): DGROUP:0x12 is 0 at 06bc-entry -> the fmap no-op-trapped (latent, not
    yet observed to crash).  Section 0xec is DELIBERATELY not installed here (patch 022: its base-lost
    device-method vectors 182a/184b are resolved directly per-patch); the twin C mid-entry FUN_1000_06e3
    (patch 031's fist_apply_reloc_section(0xec,1)) has NO callers -> dead.

FIX (faithful, patch-346 precedent -- no guard, no band-aid): drop all three base-lost far-applier
dispatches.  This mirrors patch 346, which dropped the NEAR-applier stray dispatches (0x0a/0x0e) that patch
345 had made dangerous by keeping the applier vectors live; the FAR sibling (0x12) was simply out of 346's
scope.  For 4b16 the faithful section-0x274 install remains (shim, unchanged) -> net behaviour identical.
For 4f6e/06bc the section is installed nowhere else and the dispatch never installed it faithfully anyway,
so dropping preserves the current (passing) behaviour and removes the flake -- the same deliberate
"don't install a section whose base-lost vectors would run on garbage" strategy patch 022 already applied to
section 0xec.  re_out/*.c stays pristine; correction via patch only.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin
(f842 0xf842..0xf85e; 4b16 0x14b16; 4f6e 0x14f6e..0x14f77; 06bc 0x106e8).

VERIFY: boot repro (multiple flows, ASLR-on) 0 SEGV over 900+ boots (was ~1-2.6%); no regression on the 36
verify.sh flows native + wasm.
